  "version": 1,
  "description": "Where a video's edit list opens and what that does to the conform verdict: src-tauri/src/mp4box.rs + conform.rs evaluate (cargo test edit_start_vectors_match_kb) and kblib/mp4box.py + kblib/conform.py (test_edit_start_vectors) replay these cases. Each movie is one video track built box by box (tests/mp4synth.py, mp4box.rs synth): decode deltas (stts), composition offsets (ctts), an edit list of [segment duration in movie units, media time in media units or -1, rate], a media timescale (default 600), a movie timescale (default 1000) and the elst version (default 0). The verdict is judged from the edit start alone, over an otherwise clean file.",
  "rule": [
    "Zero-length empty edits are dropped. No edit left: none. Several segments, an empty edit or a rate other than 1: complex.",
    "Otherwise the one edit's media time against the sorted composition times: equal to the first is first-frame, earlier is gap, equal to a later one is frame, between two is mid-sample.",
    "none and first-frame leave the verdict ok. Any other start is an edit list (suspect, conform recommended); mid-sample adds edit-mid-sample and makes the verdict ffmpeg-misdecodes, since ffmpeg drops that frame and shows the next one at 0 s."
  ],
